WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.779 --> 00:00:10.320
Comparison is where course thinking gets real. This page holds two or three sources next to each other so you can see what each one argues.

2
00:00:10.321 --> 00:00:17.181
Pick two or three sources. Choose sources that speak to the same question from different angles.

3
00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:24.470
Read the side-by-side panels. Each panel keeps the source's own argument, evidence, and limits visible.

4
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:35.176
Press Synthesize when you are ready. The synthesis builds a layered frame across your chosen sources. Use it as a thinking scaffold, not as sentences to copy.

5
00:00:35.176 --> 00:00:43.646
Write your own take in the notes box. One or two sentences in your own words is worth more than the whole generated frame.

6
00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:48.888
Comparisons are never graded. They exist to sharpen your written work.

7
00:00:48.888 --> 00:00:55.629
Where next: Carry your comparison insight into this week's reflection or your next assignment.
